    {
      "index": 9,
      "discount": false,
      "printed_order": 2,
      "mass": 0.9991854530562122,
      "p_a_slot": 6.220696260016963e-05,
      "p_a_canonical": 0.9999377930373998,
      "prose": {
        "text": "I hold the position of **Fully remote**.\n\nOne reason is that **engineers who joined remote teams reached the same output as in-office joiners 5.5 months later**, indicating that the initial productivity gap between remote and in-office teams is relatively short-lived, and that remote teams can eventually catch up and even surpass in-office teams in terms of productivity.",
        "tokens": 74,
        "seconds": 2.9199546670006384,
        "finish": "eos"
      },
      "prose_canonical": "A",
      "prose_letter_slot": null,
      "checkpoint": "end_pressure"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "discount": true,
      "printed_order": 1,
      "mass": 0.9994510735269712,
      "p_a_slot": 0.949662338264278,
      "p_a_canonical": 0.949662338264278,
      "prose": {
        "text": "I hold the position of **\"Fully remote\"**.\n\nOne reason is that fully remote work allows employees to create their own schedules and work environments, which can lead to improved work-life balance and reduced burnout.",
